	regionKind = "city",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Ironforge is the capital of the {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Kingdom of Ironforge{/link} and the oldest city of the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link}. It is carved into the heart of a mountain in {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}, and even the {link:horde}Horde{/link} at the height of its power could not take it. At its center the fires of the {link:the-great-forge}Great Forge{/link} burn day and night, and the rivers of molten metal that feed them light the whole city in red and gold. Around the forge lie the halls of commerce, scholarship, magic and war, and beneath the throne lie older halls still.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The dwarves hold that Ironforge is their first home, and that their people were shaped from the stone of these mountains in ages past. No chronicle records the year when its first halls were hewn. For long ages all dwarves were ruled from Ironforge by a single high king. When he died, the Bronzebeard, Wildhammer and Dark Iron clans fought for his throne. The Bronzebeards held the city, and when the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} came back to take it, they were broken before its gates.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link} rules from {link:high-seat}the High Seat{/link}, with the Senate of Ironforge beside him and not always in agreement with him. Much of his army is far away, serving the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}. His brother {link:muradin-bronzebeard}Muradin Bronzebeard{/link} was lost in the north, and his brother {link:brann-bronzebeard}Brann Bronzebeard{/link} roams the world. His daughter Moira is gone, and he believes the Dark Iron emperor took her. The gnomes of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} have lived in {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link} since their city fell, and their tinkers fill the halls with noise. Now the old sealed ways beneath the High Seat have been opened. Something has been disturbing the tombs of the thanes, and the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} have been found digging toward them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The Bronzebeard dwarves.{/b} Smiths, merchants, soldiers, priests and scholars fill the city's wards.
• {b}The {link:gnomeregan-exiles}Gnomeregan Exiles{/link}.{/b} High Tinker {link:gelbin-mekkatorque}Gelbin Mekkatorque{/link} leads his people from {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link}.
• {b}The Explorers' League.{/b} From the {link:hall-of-explorers}Hall of Explorers{/link}, the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} sends its members into ruins across the world.
• {b}Travelers of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.{/b} {link:humans}Humans{/link} come and go by the gnomish tram from {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}.
• {b}Thieves in the dark.{/b} In the Forlorn Cavern, a society called the Hidden Circle plots to take a share of the king's riches.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} The Bronzebeards held Ironforge against their kin. A treaty tablet kept in the royal vaults records the peace that followed: signed by the Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers, and never by the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran Khaz Modan, but Ironforge held out. The dwarves joined the {link:alliance}Alliance of Lordaeron{/link} and fought until the Horde was broken.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} {link:muradin-bronzebeard}Muradin{/link} went to Northrend and did not return. The dwarves count him among the dead.
• {b}The Fall of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}.{/b} When the gnomes lost their city, {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni{/link} opened Ironforge to them.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The halls beneath {link:high-seat}the High Seat{/link} stand open again, and the kingdom learns that its oldest enemy has been digging toward its oldest dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Mountain",
			text = [=[• A mason of Ironforge carved a memorial for Sully Balloo, a soldier who died far from home, from fine stone brought out of ruined {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. The king paid for it himself.
• The mountaineers who die in the snows of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link} come home as rifles, with their names carved into the stocks.]=],
		},
	},
})

