	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Muradin Bronzebeard is the brother of {link:magni-bronzebeard}King Magni{/link}. He was one of the mightiest warriors of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}, a {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} of great strength, blunt speech and a warm heart. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} he went to the frozen continent of Northrend, and he did not come home. Ironforge counts him among its dead.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Muradin was bound to the house of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} by more than alliance. He had been a teacher in arms to the young Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link}, and the two were friends. That bond made Muradin a witness to the prince's first steps toward ruin. It also cost him his life, or so it is believed in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He served the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and was known in the courts of the human kingdoms.
• He taught the prince of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} the craft of the sword and the hammer.
• He led an expedition of dwarves to Northrend in search of a legendary runeblade called Frostmourne.
• He fought beside {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link} against the undead in the frozen wastes.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Journey North",
			text = [=[Muradin's company had searched Northrend for Frostmourne for a long time before they met {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas{/link}, who had followed a dreadlord across the sea. The dwarves and the prince joined forces against the undead. Muradin grew uneasy as he watched his old pupil. Arthas had burned his own ships so that his men could not go home, and his hatred of the enemy had become the only thing he seemed to live for.

At last they found the blade in a frozen cavern, sealed in ice and guarded. Muradin read the warning carved there and begged Arthas to leave it. The prince would not. When Arthas freed the sword, the ice burst apart, and a shard of it struck Muradin down. Arthas took Frostmourne and went on without him.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In Ironforge",
			text = [=[The dwarves remember Muradin as a hero of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the brother of their king. His loss is one more weight that {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni{/link} carries, beside an army far from home and a daughter taken by the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}. In the halls of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} his name is spoken with sorrow, and with the stubborn pride that dwarves keep for those who fell doing what they thought was right.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[What became of Muradin after that day is not known in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. His people believe he died in the ice. No chronicle known to the dwarves records otherwise.]=],
		},
	},
	bonds = {
