		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Mekkatorque holds the gnomes together. Without him, the exiles would be a crowd of refugees. With him, they remain a nation, with a seat among the peoples of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and a claim to their city that they have never given up.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He led the gnomes of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} as High Tinker.
• When the troggs rose beneath the city, he turned the gnomes' own arts against them in a desperate purge, and the city was poisoned.
• He led the survivors to {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} and made {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link} their home.
• He sends volunteers back into Gnomeregan to recover what was left behind, and to strike at the traitor who holds it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Fall of the City",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the troggs came up from the depths beneath {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}. They came in great numbers, and the city could not hold them back. Mekkatorque chose to purge them with a weapon of the gnomes' own making. It killed troggs, but it also killed a great many gnomes, and it left the city soaked in poison. Many of those who lived were changed into sick and witless lepers. The rest fled into the snows of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Court in Exile",
			text = [=[In {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link}, the High Tinker's people have not stopped working. Tinkmaster Overspark hopes to repair his poor Techbot, whose mind was reversed in the fall. Master Mechanic Castpipe organizes parties to recover vital records from the city's terminals. Klockmort Spannerspan needs the parts that no one remembered to take in the flight. Every such mission is a small step back into {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}, and Mekkatorque encourages them all.]=],
		},
	},
	chapters = {
		{
			key = "the-grand-betrayal",
			title = "The Grand Betrayal",
			hint = "Strike down the traitor who rules Gnomeregan.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 2929 },
			},
			text = [=[Mekkatorque had trusted {link:mekgineer-thermaplugg}Sicco Thermaplugg{/link}. He had never imagined that Thermaplugg would betray him and the whole gnomish people, and he still does not understand why, for power and wealth would have come to Thermaplugg in time. Now the traitor sits in the ruins, the king of nothing. When word came that Thermaplugg had fallen, Mekkatorque allowed himself a grim joke, and then turned his mind to the day the gnomes would take their city back.]=],
		},
	},
	mentions = {
		{
			text = "Data Rescue",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 2930 },
			},
		},
		{
			text = "Save Techbot's Brain!",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 2922 },
			},
		},
		{
			text = "Essential Artificials",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 2924 },
			},
		},
	},
	bonds = {
		{ id = "mekgineer-thermaplugg", name = "Mekgineer Thermaplugg", note = "the traitor" },
		{ id = "magni-bronzebeard", name = "Magni Bronzebeard", note = "his host and ally" },
		{ id = "razzle-sprysprocket", name = "Razzle Sprysprocket", note = "one of his people seeking a cure" },
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "figure",
	id = "royal-historian-archesonus",
	title = "Royal Historian Archesonus",
	aliases = { "Archesonus" },
	subtitle = "Royal Historian of Ironforge",
	tier = "B",
	region = "ironforge",
	npc = { 8879 },
	allegiance = "Kingdom of Ironforge",
	found = "The High Seat, beside the throne",
	pin = { x = 38.4, y = 55.3 },
	unlock = {
		{ type = "interact" },
	},
	hint = [=[Speak with the historian who keeps the kingdom's memory beside the throne.]=],
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Royal Historian Archesonus keeps the memory of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} beside the throne of {link:magni-bronzebeard}King Magni{/link}. Any who ask may hear from her the history of the kingdom. The tale she tells most gravely is that of the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}, and of the city of {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link}, which burned.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Archesonus is the voice of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}'s past. The dwarves are a people of long memory, and in {link:high-seat}the High Seat{/link} that memory has a keeper. Her knowledge of the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} has become urgent, for the kingdom's old enemy is on the move again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• She teaches the history of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} to those who come to {link:high-seat}the High Seat{/link}.
• She sends searchers to {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}the ruins of Thaurissan{/link} in the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link} to read the relics left there.]=],
		},
	},
	chapters = {
		{
			key = "the-story-of-thaurissan",
			title = "The Story of Thaurissan",
			hint = "Ask the Royal Historian for the history of the Dark Irons.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 3702 },
			},
			text = [=[Archesonus begins far back, when the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} had a city of their own. {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} stood in a green country that is now the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}, and in those days the dwarven clans were at war with one another. Then a terrible blast destroyed it, and the land for miles around was burned to cinders. What caused the blast, she admits, no historian can say. The Dark Irons who lived went into the mountain and began again. From the ashes rose {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} Spire, and {link:the-cauldron}the Cauldron{/link} of {link:searing-gorge}the Searing Gorge{/link} was fortified. Soon there were whispers of an ancient evil that ruled the Dark Iron kingdom from within. Her tale ends in the present. The Dark Irons are seen more often on the surface every year. They have raised forts in the {link:badlands}Badlands{/link}, sent great parties into {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link} and even attacked the dam of {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			key = "the-smoldering-ruins",
			title = "The Smoldering Ruins",
			hint = "Read the relics of Thaurissan and bring their memories home.",
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 3701 },
			},
			text = [=[The relics of the ruined city hold memories, and the ones who touch them keep them. A creature of pure flame. Eight Dark Iron dwarves at a ritual. One of them alone at the end, kneeling amid seven dead before a pillar of fire. Archesonus heard these memories and said that they explained a great deal, and that there was much more to learn.]=],
		},
	},
	mentions = {
		{
			text = [=[The Smoldering {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Ruins of Thaurissan{/link}]=],
			unlock = {
				{ type = "quest", id = 3701 },
			},
		},
	},
	bonds = {
		{ id = "magni-bronzebeard", name = "Magni Bronzebeard", note = "her king" },
	},
})

Add({
